{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'CD14-positive|CD14-negative|CD16-positive|CD16-negative|CD11c-negative|CD123-positive' src/ontology/cl-edit.owl\"","aggregated_output":"4173:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000042 \"These cells are CD11b-negative, CD15-negative, CD16-negative, CD35-negative, CD49d-positive, CD68-positive, lactotransferrin-negative, and fMLP receptor-negative. They are found in the Band 3 fraction.\")\n4715:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009504\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11138776\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12560239\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7880385\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000096 \"A fully differentiated neutrophil, a granular leukocyte having a nucleus with three to five lobes connected by slender threads, and cytoplasm containing fine inconspicuous granules and stainable by neutral dyes. They are produced in bone marrow at a rate of 5e10-10e10/day and have a half-life of 6-8 hours. Neutrophils are CD15-positive, CD16-positive, CD32-positive, CD43-positive, CD181-positive, and CD182-positive.\")\n5062:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23616747\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000129 \"Unlike macroglial cells, microglial cells  arise from hematopoietic stem cells in the yolk sac during early embryogenesis that populate the central nervous system. They derive from embryonic mesoderm and are not from neuroectoderm where glioblast develops from. Markers: Mouse: CD11b+, F4/80+, CD68+. They represent ~12% of the cells in the CNS, but they are not uniformly distributed within the CNS. A normal adult mouse brain has approximately 3.5x10e6 microglia. Microglia are also reportedly CD3-negative, CD4-positive, CD8-negative, CD11b-positive, CD11c-high, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD45-low, CD56-negative, CD163-negative, CD200R-positive, CD281-positive, CD282-positive, CD283-positive, CD284-positive, CD285-positive, CD286-positive, CD287-positive, CD288-positive, CD289-positive, Gr1-negative, nestin-positive, and PU.1-positive.\")\n5117:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000134 \"Many but not all mesenchymal cells derive from the mesoderm. MSCs are reportedly CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD5-negative, CD8-negative, CD11a-negative, CD11b-negative, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD29-positive, CD31-negative, CD34-negative, CD38-negative, CD40-negative, CD44-positive, CD45-negative, CD49-positive, CD54-positive, CD66b-negative, CD79a-negative, CD80-negative, CD102-positive, CD106-positive, CD117-positive, CD121a-positive, CD121b-positive, CD123-positive, CD124-positive, CD133-negative, CD146-positive, CD166-positive, CD271-positive, B220-negative, Gr1-negative, MHCI-positive, MHCII-negative, SSEA4-negative, sca1-positive, Ter119-negative, and glycophorin A-negative. Cultured MSCs are capable of producing stem cell factor, IL7, IL8, IL11, TGF-beta, cofilin, galectin-1, laminin-receptor 1, cyclophilin A, and MMP-2.\")\n5128:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000135 \"Cultured human fibrocytes are MHCI-positive, MHCII-positive, CD1a-negative, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD8-negative, CD10-negative, CD11b-positive, CD13-positive, CD14-negative, CD16-negative, CD18-positive, CD19-negative, CD25-negative, CD29-positive, CD32-positive, CD33-negative, CD34-positive, CD38-negative, CD40-positive, CD44-negative, CD45RO-positive, CD49a-positive, CD49b-positive, CD49c-negative, CD49d-negative, CD49e-positive, CD49f-negative, CD56-negative, CD58-positive, CD61-positive, CD64-positive, CD70-negative, CD71-positive, CD80-positive, CD83-negative, CD86-positive, CD103-negative, CD105-positive, CD181-positive, CD182-negative, CD183-positive, CD184-positive, CD185-negative, CD186-negative, CD191-positive, CD192-negative, CD193-positive, CD194-positive, CD195-positive, CD196-negative, CD197-positive, CD199-positive, desmin-negative, F4/80-positive, Gr1-positive, LSP-1-positive, MHCI-positive, MHCII-positive, alpha-SMA-negative, TCRab-negative, TCRgd-negative, and vimentin-positive. Fibrocytes are also capable of secreting angiogenin, bFGF, CCL2, CCL3, CCL4, CCL8, CXCL1, type I collagen, type III collagen, CTGF, fibronectin, GM-CSF, IL-1a, IL-6, IL-8, IL-10, M-CSF, MMP-9, PDGF-A, TGF-alpha, TGF-beta1, TNF-alpha, and VEGF-A.\")\n6018:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000233 \"Platelets are reportedly CCR1-positive, CCR2-negative, CCR3-positive, CCR4-positive, CCR5-negative, CCR6-negative, CCR7-negative, CCR8-negative, CCR9-negative, CCR10-negative, CD16-positive, CD23-positive, CD32-positive, CD40-positive, CD41-positive CD42-positive, CD61-positive, CD62P-positive, CD64-positive, CD89-positive, CD102-positive, CD147-positive (activated platelets), CD154-positive (activated platelets), CD162-positive, CD209, CD282-positive, CD284-positive, CD289-positive, CD181-negative, CD182-negative, CD183-negative, CD184-positive, CLEC2-positive, GPVI-positive, JAMC-positive, PAR1-positive, PAR2-negative, PAR3-positive, PAR4-positive, TSP1-positive, and TXA2R-positive. Platelets can reportedly produce CCL2, CCL3, CCL5, CCL7, CCL17, CD40L, CXCL1, CXCL4, CXCL4L1, CXCL5, CXCL7, CXCL8, CXCL12, EGF, factor V, factor VII, factor XI, factor XIII, bFGF, histamine, IGF-1, IL-1beta, PAI-1, PDGF, plasminogen, protein S, serotonin, TGF-beta, TFPI, VEGF, and vWF.\")\n7654:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000453 \"Originally described in the dendritic cell ontology (DC_CL:0000021 )(PMID:19243617). These cells are also CD1a-high, CD14-negative, CD207-positive (langerin), CD324-positive (E-cadherin), and DCIR-positive. They reside in the epidermis.\")\n8503:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000553 \"Lineage negative is described here as CD2-negative, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD5-negative, CD8a-negative, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD20-negative, CD56-negative, Ly6g-negative, and Ter119-negative.\")\n8539:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D055014\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2213186\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC548021\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16647566\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CFU-GM\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000557 \"A hematopoietic progenitor cell that is committed to the granulocyte and monocyte lineages. These cells are CD123-positive, and do not express Gata1 or Gata2 but do express C/EBPa, and Pu.1.\")\n8547:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000557 \"Originally described in the dendritic cell ontology (DC_CL:0000042)(PMID:19243617). GMPs are reportedly CD16-positive, CD32-positive, CD34-positive, CD38-positive, CD45RA-positive, CD110-negative, CD117-positive, CD123-positive, and SCA1-negative.\")\n8627:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000564 \"These cells are CD11b-negative, CD15-positive, CD16-negative, CD49d-positive, CD68-positive, CD35-negative, and fMLP receptor-negative. They are found in the Band 3 fraction.\")\n8775:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10618520\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12560239\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000580 \"A neutrophil precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a promyelocyte and a metamyelocyte; in this stage, production of primary granules is complete and neutrophil-specific granules has started. No nucleolus is present. This cell type is CD13-positive, CD16-negative, integrin alpha-M-positive, CD15-positive, CD33-positive, CD24-positive, C/EBP-a-positive, C/EBPe-positive, PU.1-positive, lactotransferrin-positive, myeloperoxidase-positive and NGAL-positive.\")\n8797:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10618520\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12560239\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000582 \"A neutrophil precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a myelocyte and the band form neutrophil. The protein synthesis seen in earlier stages decreases or stops; the nucleus becomes indented where the indentation is smaller than half the distance to the farthest nuclear margin; chromatin becomes coarse and clumped; specific granules predominate while primary granules are rare; and the cytoplasm becomes amphophilic like that of a mature granulocyte. This cell type is integrin alpha-M-positive, CD13-negative, CD15-positive, CD16-positive, CD33-positive, CD24-positive, fMLP receptor-negative and has expression of C/EBP-a, C/EBP-e, PU.1 transcription factor, lactotransferrin, myeloperoxidase and neutrophil gelatinase associated lipocalin.\")\n9064:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19622087\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.cap.org\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000612 \"A eosinophil precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a promyelocyte and a metamyelocyte;in this stage, production of primary granules is complete and eosinophil-specific granules has started. No nucleolus is present. These cells are integrin alpha-M-positive, CD13-positive, CD15-positive, CD16-negative, CD24-positive, and CD33-positive.\")\n10423:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D001491\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2626675\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11927641\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19741522\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21236338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9933081\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000767 \"Any of the immature or mature forms of a granular leukocyte that in its mature form has an irregularly shaped, pale-staining nucleus that is partially constricted into two lobes, and with cytoplasm that contains coarse, bluish-black granules of variable size. Basophils contain vasoactive amines such as histamine and serotonin, which are released on appropriate stimulation. A basophil is CD123-positive, CD193-positive, CD203c-positive, and FceRIa-positive.\")\n10431:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000767 \"Matures in the bone marrow and account for <1% of leukocytes in the peripheral blood, spleen, and bone marrow. Basophils are described as being CD11a-positive, CD11b-positive, CD13-positive, CD15-positive, CD18-positive, CD21-positive, CD25-positive, CD29-positive, CD35-positive, CD40-positive, CD40L-positive, CD44-positive, CD45R-negative, CD46-positive, CD49a-positive, CD49b-positive, CD49d-positive, CD55-positive, CD59-positive, CD62L-positive, CD63-positive, CD69-positive, CD90-negative, CD116-positive, CD117-negative, CD124-positive, CD125-positive, CD131-positive, CD161-positive, CD184-positive, CD191-positive, CD192-positive, CD197-positive, CD200R3-positive, CD218-positive, CD282-positive, CD284-positive, CD289-positive, CD290-positive, CD294-positive, natural killer cell receptor 2B4-positive, smad1-positive, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD7-negative, CD8-negative, CD14-negative, CD15-negative, CD16-negative, CD19-negative, CD20-negative, CD34-negative, CD36-negative, CD45R-negative, CD56-negative, CD57-negative, CD235a-negative, and GR1-negative. Transcription factors- GATA1-positive, PU.1-positive.\")\n10448:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18466030\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000769 \"A basophil precursor in the granulocytic series, being a cell intermediate in development between a basophilic myelocyte and a band form basophil. The nucleus becomes indented where the indentation is smaller than half the distance to the farthest nuclear margin; chromatin becomes coarse and clumped; specific granules predominate while primary granules are rare. Markers are CD11b-positive, CD15-positive, CD16-positive, CD24-positive, CD33-positive, and CD13-positive.\")\n10477:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000771 \"Eosinophils are also CD14-negative, CD32-positive, CD44-positive, CD48-positive, CD69-positive, CD192-negative, MBP1-positive, MBP2-positive, TLR2-negative, TLR4-negative, and lineage-negative (B220, CD2, CD14, CD19, CD56, CD71, CD117, CD123, CD235a (glycophorin A), and TER119). The cytokines IL-3, IL-5, and GM-CSF are involved in their development and differentiation. Usually considered CD16-negative, CD16 is observed on eosinophilic metamyelocyte.\")\n10600:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000782 \"These cells are CD1a-negative, CD1b-positive, CD11a-positive, CD11c-positive, CD13-positive, CD14-negative, CD20-negative, CD21-negative, CD33-positive, CD40-negative, CD50-positive, CD54-positive, CD58-positive, CD68-negative, CD80-negative, CD83-negative, CD85j-positive, CD86-positive, CD89-negative, CD95-positive, CD120a-negative, CD120b-positive, CD123-negative, CD178-negative, CD206-negative, CD207-negative, CD209-negative, and TNF-alpha-negative. Upon TLR stimulation, they are capable of producing high levels of TNF-alpha, IL-6, CXCL8 (IL-8).\")\n10614:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2118448\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC538703\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15549123\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17332250\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17850486\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20304825\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000784 \"A dendritic cell type of distinct morphology, localization, and surface marker expression (CD123-positive) from other dendritic cell types and associated with early stage immune responses, particularly the release of physiologically abundant amounts of type I interferons in response to infection.\")\n11255:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000831 \"MCP are CD16-positive, CD32-positive, CD34-positive, CD45-positive, integrin beta-7-positive, and lin-negative (CD2, CD3e, CD4, CD5, CD8a, CD14, CD19, CD20, CD27, integrin alpha-M, ly6c, ly6g, NCAM-1, and ter119). These cells also express the transcription factors GATA-1, GATA-2, and MITF, but not C/EBPa.\")\n12420:# Class: obo:CL_0000938 (CD16-negative, CD56-bright natural killer cell, human)\n12422:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19796267\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000938 \"NK cell that has the phenotype CD56-bright, CD16-negative, and CD84-positive with the function to secrete interferon-gamma but is not cytotoxic.\")\n12424:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000938 \"CD16-negative, CD56-bright NK cell\")\n12428:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000938 \"CD16-negative, CD56-bright natural killer cell, human\")\n12431:# Class: obo:CL_0000939 (CD16-positive, CD56-dim natural killer cell, human)\n12433:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19796267\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000939 \"A mature natural killer cell that has the phenotype CD56-low, CD16-positive and which is capable of cytotoxicity and cytokine production.\")\n12435:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000939 \"CD16-positive, CD56-dim NK cell\")\n12436:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000939 \"CD16-positive, CD56-low NK cell\")\n12437:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000939 \"CD16-positive, CD56-low natural killer cell\")\n12438:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000939 \"CD16-positive, CD56-positive NK cell\")\n12439:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000939 \"CD16-positive, CD56-positive natural killer cell\")\n12443:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000939 \"CD16-positive, CD56-dim natural killer cell, human\")\n12473:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19941119\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000942 \"A plasmacytoid dendritic cell developing in the thymus with phenotype CD11c-negative or low, CD45RA-positive, CD11b-negative, and CD123-positive.\")\n12979:# Class: obo:CL_0000991 (CD11c-negative plasmacytoid dendritic cell)\n12981:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15771572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17850486\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19243617\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29313948\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000991 \"CD11c-negative plasmacytoid dendritic cell is a leukocyte is CD11c-negative, CD45RA-positive, CD85g-positive(ILT7), CD123-positive, CD303-positive.\")\n12984:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000991 \"CD11c-negative plasmacytoid dendritic cell\")\n13007:# Class: obo:CL_0000994 (immature CD11c-negative plasmacytoid dendritic cell)\n13009:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15771572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17850486\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000994 \"Immature CD11c-negative plasmacytoid dendritic cell is a CD11c-negative plasmacytoid dendritic cell is CD80-negative, CD86-low and MHCII-low.\")\n13011:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000994 \"immature CD11c-negative plasmacytoid dendritic cell\")\n13024:# Class: obo:CL_0000996 (mature CD11c-negative plasmacytoid dendritic cell)\n13026:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15771572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17850486\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000996 \"Mature CD11c-negative plasmacytoid dendritic cell is a CD11c-negative plasmacytoid dendritic cell is CD80-high, CD86-high, MHCII-high and is CD83-positive.\")\n13028:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000996 \"mature CD11c-negative plasmacytoid dendritic cell\")\n13339:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001029 \"Surface markers are for mouse cells. Originally described in the dendritic cell ontology (DC_CL:0000041) CDP are reportedly CD2-negative, CD3-negative, CD4-negative, CD5-negative, CD8a-negative, CD11c-positive, CD14-negative, CD19-negative, CD20-negative, CD56-negative, B220-negative, Ly6g-negative, MHCII-positive, and Ter119-negative. (PMID:19243617).\")\n13574:# Class: obo:CL_0001054 (CD14-positive monocyte)\n13579:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001054 \"CD14-positive monocyte\")\n13583:# Class: obo:CL_0001055 (CD14-positive, CD16-low monocyte)\n13585:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20628149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001055 \"An intermediate monocyte that is CD14-positive and with low amounts of CD16.\")\n13588:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001055 \"CD14-positive, CD16-low monocyte\")\n13612:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001058 \"A plasmacytoid dendritic cell with the phenotype HLA-DRA-positive, CD123-positive, and CD11c-negative.\")\n13630:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001059 \"CMP are reportedly CD16-positive, CD32-positive, CD38-positive, CD45RA-negative, CD110-negative, CD117-positive, CD123-positive, and SCA1-negative.\")\n14235:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002028 \"There may be an intermediate cell type. These cells also CD13-positive, CD16-positive, CD32-positive, and integrin beta 7-positive. Transcription factors: GATA1-positive, MCP-1-positive, mitf-positive, PU.1-positive, and CEBP/a-low.\")\n14569:# Class: obo:CL_0002057 (CD14-positive, CD16-negative classical monocyte)\n14571:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15615263\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1706877\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19689341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002057 \"A classical monocyte that is CD14-positive, CD16-negative, CD64-positive, CD163-positive.\")\n14575:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002057 \"CD16-negative monocyte\")\n14577:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002057 \"CD14-positive, CD16-negative classical monocyte\")\n17745:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:14568979\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19800965\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002343 \"A natural killer cell subset that is found in the decidual of the uterus and is CD56-high, Galectin-1-positive and CD16-negative. This cell type represents the most abundant immune cell type in the decidual during the first trimester of pregnancy.\")\n18268:# Class: obo:CL_0002396 (CD14-low, CD16-positive monocyte)\n18270:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20870168\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002396 \"A patrolling monocyte that is CD14-low and CD16-positive.\")\n18275:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002396 \"CD14-low, CD16-positive monocyte\")\n18280:# Class: obo:CL_0002397 (CD14-positive, CD16-positive monocyte)\n18282:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20628149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21937707\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22343568\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002397 \"A CD14-positive monocyte that is also CD16-positive and CCR2-negative.\")\n18287:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002397 \"CD14-positive, CD16-positive monocyte\")\n19005:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002467 \"A myeloid suppressor cell that is Gr1-high and CD11c-negative.\")\n19075:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002474 \"A MHC-II-negative classical monocyte located in lymphoid tissue that is F4/80-positive, CD11c-negative, and CD11b-high.\")\n19574:# Class: obo:CL_0002526 (CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell)\n19576:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19236899\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20309010\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002526 \"A dermal dendritic cell that is CD1a-negative and CD14-positive.\")\n19579:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002526 \"CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell\")\n19583:# Class: obo:CL_0002527 (immature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell)\n19585:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002527 \"An immature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell is CD80-low, CD86-low, and MHCII-low.\")\n19586:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002527 \"immature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell\")\n19590:# Class: obo:CL_0002528 (mature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell)\n19592:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002528 \"A mature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell is CD80-high, CD86-high, MHCII-high and is CD83-positive.\")\n19593:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002528 \"mature CD14-positive dermal dendritic cell\")\n19600:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20309010\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002529 \"A dermal dendritic cell that is CD1a-positive and CD14-negative.\")\n19622:# Class: obo:CL_0002532 (CD16-positive myeloid dendritic cell)\n19624:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17332250\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002532 \"A myeloid dendritic cell found in the blood that is CD16-positive.\")\n19628:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002532 \"CD16-positive myeloid dendritic cell\")\n19632:# Class: obo:CL_0002533 (immature CD16-positive myeloid dendritic cell)\n19634:AnnotationAssertion(Anno